swift-sheet-music
=================

This Swift package provides libraries for working with engraved music
notation: parsing MuseScore (.mscx) files, modelling them as Swift value
types, and exporting them to MIDI. It is an unofficial implementation,
not affiliated with or endorsed by MuseScore Limited / Muse Group, nor
with Apple's `MusicKit` framework.

Source code license
-------------------

The Swift source code under `Sources/` (libraries `SheetMusic`,
`SheetMusicCore`, `SheetMusicMSCX`, `SheetMusicMIDI`) is licensed under
the MIT License (see LICENSE in the project root).

The implementation is independently authored. Algorithms (e.g. arpeggio
note timing, pause-aware tempo map handling, MeasureRepeat group
resolution, Volta-aware repeat playback) were studied from the MuseScore
C++ implementation (https://github.com/musescore/MuseScore, GPL-3.0) but
no source code is copied; the Swift implementation was rewritten from
scratch using the referenced behaviour as a specification. Inline doc
comments occasionally cross-reference the originating MuseScore class or
function for traceability.

MuseScore is a trademark of Muse Group. Use of the name in this project's
documentation and code identifiers is nominative (to indicate file format
and behavioural compatibility) and does not imply affiliation.

MuseScore submodule
-------------------

The `MuseScore/` git submodule references the upstream MuseScore source
repository (GPL-3.0) for development convenience: it allows the Swift
implementation to be cross-referenced against the C++ source. The
submodule is **not** redistributed as part of this Swift package: SwiftPM
consumers receive only the contents of `Sources/` (plus dependencies);
the submodule is initialised on demand via `git submodule update --init`
when cloning this repository for development.

Test fixtures
-------------

The mscx and reference MIDI files under `Tests/SheetMusicTests/Resources/`
are copies of test fixtures from the upstream MuseScore repository
(`MuseScore/src/importexport/midi/tests/midiexport_data/`), used here to
verify byte/semantic equivalence with MuseScore's own MIDI exporter output.
These files are licensed under GPL-3.0; see
`Tests/SheetMusicTests/Resources/LICENSE`.

Because these fixtures are confined to the test target and are not
distributed as part of the published library products, they do not affect
the licence of code that depends on this package.

